# The actions and rpcs of Arcana's modules (and below, the data nodes
# that hold a file's or a command line's text) that run by NACM's
# exec-default (RFC 8341), not nacm:default-deny-all: each reads what
# the host has, gives out nothing that should stay on it, runs nothing
# with arguments its caller chooses and makes the host reach nowhere.
# One a line: <module>:<path>, a tab, why (share/arcana/nacm.awk,
# make check-nacm).  A whole module is "<module>:*".

# Served by the console, not the agent: its roles decide
# (restconf_act_role(), cyang.c), and arcana-cluster's are the nodes'.
arcana-console:*	the console's own module, its roles checked by the console
arcana-cluster:*	the console nodes' family, between nodes by their certificates

arcana-bird:/daemon/read	birdc -r (restricted) show status and protocols; in a vnet jail (its own birdc, jexec) an operator's (jail_prog_refused())
arcana-bird:/daemon/routes	birdc -r show route, its words checked (route_words()); a viewer's on the host, an operator's in a vnet jail
arcana-bird:/daemon/ospf	birdc -r show ospf, a protocol's name checked; a viewer's on the host, an operator's in a vnet jail
arcana-crashes:/crashes/read	the cores' names; a backtrace (char * arguments of the core's memory) an operator's, of a crash kmsg recorded alone
arcana-events:/events/read	the agent's own events after a number
arcana-firewall:/firewall/firewall/trace	dtrace of ipfw's rule-matched for an address checked as one: the rule and the ports, no payload; a viewer's
arcana-firewall:/kept-host/from-rc	the firewall script read and turned into kept rules, nothing written; a viewer's
arcana-history:/history/read	the agent's own samples
arcana-history:/history/read-archive	the agent's own samples kept on its disk, the points of a read bounded
arcana-host:/host/read-certificates	the trusted certificates, public, parsed
arcana-jail-files://arcj:jails/read-files	jail.conf(5)'s files, as a read of running has the jails, each secret masked below an operator
arcana-jobs:/jobs/job/read	a job's trace, keys kept out of it: its argv, title and steps' details masked for every role
arcana-log:/logs/read	a log of the log directory, opened beneath a jail's root, read-only: a viewer's of the logs every user on the host may read (mode o+r) and @dmesg; the others and the audit trail an operator's
arcana-netgraph:/netgraph/read	ngctl list
arcana-netstore:/netstore/read	NFS, iSCSI and HAST as they are
arcana-network:/network/bridges	ifconfig of the bridges
arcana-network:/network/connections	the kernel's connections (pcb)
arcana-network:/network/geneve	ifconfig of the geneve interfaces
arcana-network:/network/interfaces	the interfaces as the kernel has them
arcana-network:/network/ipfw	a vnet jail's ipfw rules, read by its own ipfw (jexec): an operator's
arcana-network:/network/ipsec	swanctl's connections and SAs, never a private key; in a vnet jail (its own swanctl) an operator's
arcana-network:/network/kept-routes	rc.conf's static routes, read
arcana-network:/network/lookup	route get of an address checked as one
arcana-network:/network/multicast	ifmcstat; in a vnet jail (its own ifmcstat) an operator's
arcana-network:/network/neighbours	ARP and NDP, read
arcana-network:/network/nexthops	netstat -on
arcana-network:/network/nhgroups	netstat -On
arcana-network:/network/routes	the routing tables
arcana-network:/network/sockets	the kernel's sockets (pcb)
arcana-probe:/probes/read	the probes' samples
arcana-processes:/processes/process/read	a process's files and threads (procstat), no environment
arcana-services:/services/service/read	service <name> enabled, status, describe, extracommands, an operator's; a viewer told what the collector saw, no script run (ira/services.c)
arcana-services://arcj:jails/arcj:jail/services/read	a running jail's scripts (read in the jail by the helper attached to it) and service -j <jail> status, describe, extracommands, an operator's; a viewer told what the collector saw, no script run; the variables an admin's alone (ira/services.c)
arcana-smtpd:/smtpd/read	OpenSMTPD's configuration and tables, secrets left out, the rest's masked below an operator; its state (service smtpd onestatus, smtpctl) an operator's, a viewer's what the watch last saw
arcana-speeder:/speeder/read	the relays, read; their log's -k masked below an operator
arcana-sslproxy:/sslproxy/read	SSLproxy's service, configuration, CA certificates and request, and ipfw's set 27, read; the CA's key never
arcana-sshd:/sshd/read	sshd's configuration and keys' fingerprints, public; a key's command= masked below an operator
arcana-storage:/storage/read	disks, pools, datasets, mounts, read; a keylocation's token, fstab's secrets masked below an operator
arcana-suricata:/suricata/command	one of the instance's read commands, from a fixed list
arcana-suricata:/suricata/read-profiling	what profiling wrote, read
arcana-suricata:/suricata/read-rules	a page of the ruleset's rules
arcana-suricata:/suricata/read-sources	suricata-update's cached index and the sources' names and states, no secret code; a source's url its host alone below an operator
arcana-sysctl:/sysctl/read	the kernel's values by name; a vnet jail's by its own sysctl (jexec), an operator's
arcana-troubleshoot:/troubleshoot/path-check	what the host would do with a packet, nothing sent
arcana-troubleshoot:/troubleshoot/traceroute	one numeric traceroute to an address checked as one: probes, no connection, nothing fetched; a viewer's
arcana-wireguard:/wireguard/read	wg show dump, the keys left out; in a vnet jail (its own wg) an operator's

# The data nodes that hold a file's or a command line's text, read by
# every role (nacm.awk): what is done of a secret in each.  A
# configuration node is not masked, its read making a candidate the
# mask would be written back from: it is nacm:default-deny-all.
arcana-jobs-kinds:*	the job kinds' changes: submit's and dry-run's input alone (both nacm:default-deny-all), never read back
arcana-agent:/bundle/file/text	the bundle grouping: config-export's output and config-apply's input, both nacm:default-deny-all
arcana-builder:/builder/make-conf/text	poudriere's make.conf files, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-builder:/builder/run/argv	a poudriere run's command line, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-events:/event/kmsg/text	the kernel's messages, which the host lets every user read (dmesg)
arcana-firewall:/firewall-data/kept/rule/text	an ipfw rule: addresses, ports and actions, no secret
arcana-firewall:/firewall-data/kept/text	the kept ipfw rules: addresses, ports and actions, no secret
arcana-firewall:/firewall-data/state/rule/text	an ipfw rule as the kernel has it, no secret
arcana-firewall:/kept-host/from-rc/text	the firewall script's ipfw rules, no secret
arcana-firewall:/kept-host/jail/text	a jail's kept ipfw rules, no secret
arcana-jail-files://arcj:jails/read-files/defaults/text	jail.conf's text, each secret (an exec.* token) masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-jail-files://arcj:jails/read-files/jail/text	a jail's file, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-jail-files://arcj:jails/read-files/template/text	a template's file, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-jobs:/step/argv	a step's command line, each secret masked for every role (trace_argv())
arcana-log:/logs/read/line/text	a log's line: a viewer reads only the logs every user on the host may read (log.c)
arcana-network:/socket/command	a socket's process's command name (ki_comm), no argument
arcana-sdwan:/edge-config/rules/rule/text	an SD-WAN ipfw rule the console wrote, no secret
arcana-sdwan:/edge-state/rules/counter/text	an SD-WAN ipfw rule's counters, no secret
arcana-sdwan:/sdwan/ids-instance/lua/text	a Suricata Lua script the console sent: a detection, no credential
arcana-sdwan:/sdwan/proxy-instance/named-list/text	a proxy's list of names or addresses, no secret
arcana-services:/services/service/command	the names of a script's commands (extracommands)
arcana-services:/services/service/read/command	the names of a script's commands (extracommands)
arcana-services://arcj:jails/arcj:jail/services/read/service/command	the names of a jail's script's commands (extracommands)
arcana-smtpd:/smtpd/read/table/text	a table's text, a secret table its names alone; each secret masked below an operator (ucl_mask())
arcana-sslproxy:/sslproxy/read/rule/text	an ipfw rule of set 27 as ipfw lists it, SSL inspection's fwd rules alone: addresses, ports and interfaces, no secret
arcana-sshd:/sshd/config	sshd_config's text, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-sshd:/sshd/user-ca-key/options	a CA key's options, command= and environment= masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-sshd:/sshd/user/key/options	a key's options, command= and environment= masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-storage:/storage-state/fstab/text	fstab(5)'s text, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-storage:/storage-state/mount/options	a mount's options, each secret masked below an operator (wmask())
arcana-suricata:/logged/text	the end of a profiling log of Suricata's: rules' and locks' timings
arcana-troubleshoot:/walk/step/text	what the host would do with a packet, said by the agent
arcana-troubleshoot:/walk/text	what the host would do with a packet, said by the agent
arcana-troubleshoot:/walk/uncertain/text	what the host would do with a packet, said by the agent
